# Aside demo story — exercises staging, choices, conditions, effects
# and branching endings. Written to be read, not just parsed.

title: Night Shift
author: Roxanne
start: start

== start ==
bg office_night
music fan_hum
The chair is still warm from whoever had this shift before you.
There is no one to ask about them.
monty: You're late.
show monty neutral at left
monty: That's twice this week.

* "I'm here, aren't I?" -> defiant
* You say nothing. -> quiet
    ~ let_the_quiet_stand true
* "...Sorry." -> apologetic

== defiant ==
~ aff_monty -1
monty: Being here isn't the same as showing up.
monty (tired): I've been on this stage for thirty years. I know the difference.
hide monty
-> hallway

== quiet ==
~ aff_monty +1
monty: ...
monty (quiet): Good answer.
monty: Most people fill the quiet. You didn't.
hide monty
-> hallway

== apologetic ==
~ aff_monty +1
monty: Don't apologise to me.
monty: Apologise to the one who had to cover you.
hide monty
-> cove

== hallway ==
bg west_hall
The hall runs long and dim. Somewhere behind you a fan keeps turning.
sfx footstep
roxanne: I heard the door.
show roxanne smirk at center
roxanne: You're not supposed to be back here.

* "Neither are you." -> roxy_banter
* "I'm doing my rounds." -> roxy_rounds
* Leave. -> hallway_exit

== roxy_banter ==
~ aff_roxy +2
roxanne (laughs): No. I'm not.
roxanne: But I've been here longer, so I win.
show roxanne warm at center
-> cove

== roxy_rounds ==
~ aff_roxy +1
roxanne: Rounds. Sure.
roxanne: You know what I do on my rounds? I check that you're still breathing.
-> cove

== hallway_exit ==
roxanne: Good.
roxanne (flat): Keep walking.
-> ending_cold

== cove ==
bg coves
The curtain is drawn. Something behind it is being very still.
freddy: Hm.
show freddy idle at right
freddy: You can hear me, can't you.
freddy: Most of them can't. They watch the cameras and think that's looking.

* "I can hear you." -> freddy_seen
* "Who are you?" -> freddy_name
* "I should go." -> ending_cold

== freddy_name ==
freddy: That's a longer answer than you have time for.
freddy (wry): Ask me again when you've done a week.
-> freddy_offer

== freddy_seen ==
~ saw_freddy true
~ aff_freddy +2
freddy: ...
freddy: Then stay a minute. That's all anyone ever wants, really.
-> freddy_offer

== freddy_offer ==
music music_box
freddy: There's a song that plays when the power dies.
freddy: I don't choose it. But I'm the one standing there when it stops.
freddy: Come back tomorrow, and I'll tell you the rest.
-> ending_warm

== ending_warm ==
bg office_dawn
The shift ends. 6 AM, and the lights come up like nothing happened.
Everything is exactly where it was. You are not.
~ nights_survived +1
-> END

== ending_cold ==
bg office_dawn
You leave without learning a single name.
The building doesn't mind. It has had a lot of you.
-> END

# --- planted problems for the traversal bot to find ---
# 1. nothing jumps here
== epilogue ==
The building is empty in the way that buildings are never empty.
-> END

# 2. typo: aff_montal is never written anywhere
== apologist_alt ==
~ aff_monty +1
monty: Fine.
-> hallway

* "One more thing." -> apologist_alt [if aff_montal >= 2]
